47
00:05:10,898 --> 00:05:15,249
Alex: Stage one: companies block A I agents. Why?

48
00:05:15,249 --> 00:05:21,230
Alex: Because agents skip right past display ads and ignore checkout upsells.

49
00:05:21,803 --> 00:05:29,528
Maya: Stage two: agents learn to disguise themselves as human users, turning the whole thing into an arms race.

50
00:05:29,987 --> 00:05:32,168
Alex: Stage three: the market splits.

51
00:05:32,168 --> 00:05:36,967
Alex: Companies that make money by actually selling goods let agents in.

52
00:05:36,967 --> 00:05:40,893
Alex: Companies that make money from data start charging fees.

53
00:05:40,893 --> 00:05:44,384
Alex: And the tech giants build their own agents.

54
00:05:44,841 --> 00:05:51,139
Maya: Stage four: a trusted middle layer emerges for agent identity and agent payments.

55
00:05:51,692 --> 00:05:58,589
Alex: Stage five: companies that welcome agents start stealing customers away from the companies that block them.

56
00:05:59,132 --> 00:06:07,080
Maya: Stage six: the blockers realize they are losing business, so they turn around and let agents in—on their own terms.

57
00:06:07,714 --> 00:06:13,608
